            <ArticleTitle>Nuclear cardiology, Part III: Scintigraphic evaluation of cardiac perfusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-9; quiz 172-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">After reading Part III of this series of nuclear cardiology articles, the technologist should be able to: (a) compare and contrast radiopharmaceuticals used for myocardial perfusion imaging; (b) describe imaging protocols used for detecting coronary artery disease; and (c) describe imaging patterns seen following reconstruction of myocardial images.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
